A||||13||88formula||FOCOA headers, your thoughts please.||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||11-01-2000||05:17 PM||||For you guys who have the FOCOA headers how do you like them? Did you notice a big difference in power? I am thinking of getting those headers for my 3.4-liter engine but I would like to hear your thoughts before I take the big plunge and lay down $600.<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierosound||11-01-2000||06:25 PM||||I can't say if there was any increase in power by installing the headers, as I installed them on a completely new 3.4L engine, anlog with a Borla exhaust system with hi-flow cat.  I also installed a larger TB, ported heads and ported intake manifolds to "get more in" the engine. <P>The other side of the equation would be to now get the exhaust out efficiently.  I CAN say my 3.4L goes to redline (6000rpm) with no flat spots at all.  Power and torque is smooth and high from idle to 6000 and the Fiero owners I've taken for a spin comment on the power.  Many want to build the same.<P>I can only imagine that an exhaust bottleneck would decrease the great performance from my combination.<P> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/tonys87.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/tonys87.htm</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 11-01-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000002||88formula||11-01-2000||07:54 PM||||Thanks fierosound. I have the Borla Exhaust too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||HYPTNOTiSE||11-01-2000||11:28 PM||||if you lay 600 on focoa headers and not 650 on my headers, yo momma should slap ya! J/K but i have both and my new ones are much nicer.<P>Check them out, <BR>Mike LeCompte||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||11-02-2000||08:12 AM||||I have almost the same setup of Fierosound except ported heads and have not installed my Borla yet. Like him I can't say of power increase because all came in as a package with the new engine. What I can say is that the quality and fit of FOCOA headers is excellent. Just order them soon because sometimes it takes long for them to build and deliver (7 weeks for me) if not in stock.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Shaun41178||11-02-2000||04:29 PM||||Hell I will slap you!!  Mike's Headers are nicer then the Focoas.  Bigger too I believe.  It has been awhile since I have seen the Focoa ones.  Mike does have a pair of the Focoa's so he can take a look at both and make a reasonable guess as to which ones are better for hp increases.  I should have taken a look at the Focoa ones while I was there this past weekend but the thought never occured to me.<P>Mike had his Heads ported out and the exhaust side of the head was much bigger then the stock opening and his headers were still larger then the ported exhaust ports in the head.  <P>When Mike's engine gets in and running with that 5 spd Izusu with the 3.83 FD  I expect that engine to be running in the low 15's!!.  Mike might be able to get it into the 14's cause he is a pretty good driver.  That is fast people.  It should be real close with an Integra Type R cause those things are like super quick especially with the watermellon pipe on it.  Look out imports!!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||11-02-2000||04:40 PM||||on a stock 2.8 headers are all smoke and mirrors. if you have Nitrous or a S/C you 'll notice a decnet improvement i'm sure. i can't say on a 3.4+ that it'll be better but it can't hurt.. the Hp and Tq numbers on a stockish 2.8 are +4hp and -9lbft and you'll kick yourself. granted we dont have dyno results on Hyptnos' stuff yet... your cars are HAPPY with the back pressure the factory manifolds have once they are ported. Hp sells cars Tq wins races.. just remember that... i'm not shooting down any bodys stuff.. just wait a while till we have dyno numbers... yeah your car will idle better, yeah your car will be louder. what is that.. yep smoke and mirrors. wait till Mike has a dyno sheet... then BUY his stuff and to he@@ with Focoa... they have no dyno numbers... <P>and Shaun.. HE BETTER be in the 14s!!! i was on a 2.8! with all the toys and trinkets he has he should pull 14.5! <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstsig1.jpg">    ).]<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||11-02-2000||05:05 PM||||1FST2M6, I know about your headers, I saw the dyno sheets you posted and you have done a lot with the 2.8-liter engine. I have been following your posts ever since you were a member. You have/had the Chris West headers. I think GTbastard has them now. I think I remember him posting a message about having problems with the weld leaking on the headers after they were Jet Hot coated, co8uld have been someone else though. That’s not good! The engine I want to install the headers on is very similar to fierosounds 3.4-liter engine. <P>I like the FOCOA headers because they have been around a wile and I have seen then up close. They looked to me like very high quality well built headers that fit well in the fiero engine bay. They have a reputation as being the best.<P>Thanks <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierosound||11-02-2000||07:57 PM||||Bigger is not always better.  Even in the Chev forums , when discussing headers for built-up 350 V8s, the question often comes up on whether to use headers with 1 1/2" or 1 3/4" primary pipes.  The general consensus is that headers with primary pipes that are too large for the application will cause a loss of low RPM torque.  Most often for street applications, headers with the smaller primary pies are the btter choice, while larger headers are used in bored/stroked (383ci) small blocks set up for racing.  PS - When I got my FOCOA headers, your setup was not available.||||reg||10
Z||000009||Alex4mula||11-03-2000||08:36 AM||||fierosound is right. Bigger primary tubes with a stock 2.8 or even maybe a 3.4 may not be good at all for street. I remember reading a header design book which pointed very clearly to avoid that mistake. I would preffer smaller primaries for anything except drag racing.||||reg||1
Z||000010||jlruiz67||11-03-2000||07:47 PM||||Hello all<BR>I like to know what is the problem that some people here have with FOCOA. I for one I'm thankfull for there existance, when I got my 2nd Fiero it was a basket case and they where the onlyones arrownd to help me with any info I needed (that was pre Pennock's Fiero Forum) it's kind of sad that now that we have more resources available we kick the club that has been there for all of us from the start. I like to know if they have done something that diserves the atacks that I have read here in the past and now. As far as I know they might be a bit slow but they have always been there and they supply us with products for the car that no one likes to work on but us. I hope some one can shed some light on the subject.<P>Thanks<P>PS I was a past member of FOCOA and should re new my membership but keep forgeting. ||||reg||5
Z||000011||HYPTNOTiSE||11-05-2000||12:31 AM||||Oh make sure you re-new.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Old PHOCOA PHIL PHUCK HEAD would love to have more of your money. Did you buy a performance chip from him? I heard they yeilded big performance gains? He sold stock PROMS with  stickers on them that said performance, that's what made them high performance.  He's a crook, he's slow and doesn't have good customer service. You're actually the first person i've heard of that doesn't mind even talking to him. Not a flame at you in anyway, just dont have much use for FOCOA.||||reg||1
