Z||000013||Black88GT||11-05-2000||07:40 PM||||Man I thought everyone knew about the fake prom chip thing. I believe it was Joe Wynman who discovered it was just a stock chip with a sticker on it.<P>I have heard from a reputable guy in Florida who was ripped off for about 300 bucks during Christmas time from FOCOA.  I heard that they haven't sent a newsletter in years.<P>In my own personal experience, I needed '88 ball joints once, and was referred to them.  Try to contact them.  GOOD LUCK!  And then they expect me to give them my CC number?!  If I would have given that to them, I would still be waiting for my 200 dollar upper ball joints.  Fiero Store was a little cheaper and I got them in 2 days.<P>FOCOA is a disgrace the Fiero community IMHO, they should just throw in the towel if they already haven't...<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||13
